@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Classified // Privacy Directives";
}

<section class="privacy-container mt-4">
    <header class="evidence-header border-bottom border-secondary mb-4 pb-2">
        <span class="classification-tag text-warning font-monospace small fw-bold">SECURITY CLEARANCE LEVEL: ALPHA</span>
        <h2 class="evidence-title text-light font-monospace text-uppercase fw-bold mt-2">@ViewData["Title"]</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content bg-dark border border-secondary p-4 shadow-lg text-light">
        <p class="lead text-info font-monospace mb-4">
            > INITIATING SECURE CONNECTION...<br />
            > WARNING: ALL ACTIVITIES ON THIS TERMINAL ARE MONITORED AND LOGGED.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-warning mt-4 font-monospace">1. Data Collection Protocols</h4>
        <p>
            By accessing the Case File System, you consent to the collection of standard terminal telemetry. We log your IP address, your browser agent, and exactly how many times you clicked "Edit" on a suspect's file. Do not attempt to mask your digital footprint; our cyber division is highly trained.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-warning mt-4 font-monospace">2. Chain of Custody (Data Sharing)</h4>
        <p>
            We absolutely do not sell your data to third-party advertising corporations. We are investigators, not marketers. However, your session data may be shared with authorized federal agencies, internal affairs, or the precinct captain if you misclassify evidence.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-warning mt-4 font-monospace">3. Cryptographic Cookies</h4>
        <p>
            This terminal deploys encrypted cookies to maintain your active duty session. These are digital tracking modules, not the glazed donuts currently sitting in the squad breakroom. Do not attempt to eat them.
        </p>

        <footer class="mt-5 pt-3 border-top border-secondary text-muted font-monospace small">
            End of file. If you disagree with these operational terms, step away from the keyboard and turn in your badge.
        </footer>
    </div>
</section>